// EchoQuestXR runtime -- libvrapi.so for Echo VR (Quest), implemented on OpenXR.
//
// Echo's engine (libr15.so) calls 35 VrApi functions; this file implements the 28 seen in
// play (docs/vrapi-calls.md), plus the shutdown ones. The rest of VrApi's 114 exports are
// stubs (unimplemented.c, generated by build.py) that log once and return 0.
//
//   VrApi                              OpenXR
//   Initialize                         loader init, xrCreateInstance, xrGetSystem
//   Get{Instance,Device}ExtensionsVulkan   xrGetVulkan{Instance,Device}ExtensionsKHR
//   CreateSystemVulkan                 xrCreateSession (Echo's VkInstance/VkDevice), spaces, actions
//   CreateTextureSwapChain3            xrCreateSwapchain (2D array = one layer per eye)
//   EnterVrMode / LeaveVrMode          xrBeginSession when READY / let the runtime stop it
//   WaitFrame / BeginFrame             xrWaitFrame / xrBeginFrame + acquire the swapchain image
//   GetPredictedTracking2              xrLocateViews + xrLocateSpace (head), cached per time
//   SubmitFrame2                       release the image, xrEndFrame with one projection layer
//   Get*Input*, SetHapticVibration...  actions on /interaction_profiles/oculus/touch_controller
//   PollEvent                          session state -> visibility/focus events
//
// Logs to logcat under EchoQuestXR. Properties, read at startup:
//   debug.echoquestxr.pose grip      controllers from the grip pose (default: aim, which matches VrApi)
//   debug.echoquestxr.flip 0|fov|copy   VrApi's images are bottom-up. fov: flip them by
//                                    submitting an upside-down field of view (default on Meta's
//                                    runtime); copy: copy each frame upside down into a second
//                                    swapchain (default elsewhere: SteamVR); 0: don't flip
//   debug.echoquestxr.test red|probe|redprobe   display-path diagnostics
